{"schema_version":3,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"bco:8-1","provision":"BCO 8-1","book":"bco","book_name":"Book of Church Order","abbreviation":"BCO","reference":"8-1","title":"Section 8-1","supplementary":false,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/bco/8-1/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#bco/8-1","current_text":{"html":"<p>This office is one of dignity and usefulness. The man who fills it has in Scripture different titles expressive of his various duties. As he has the oversight of the flock of Christ, he is termed <i>bishop</i> or <i>pastor</i>. As it is his duty to be spiritually fruitful, dignified, and prudent, an example to the flock, and to govern well in the house and Kingdom of Christ, he is termed <i>presbyter</i> or <i>elder</i>. As he expounds the Word, and by sound doctrine both exhorts and convinces the gainsayer, he is termed <i>teacher</i>. These titles do not indicate different grades of office, but all describe one and the same office.</p>","text":"This office is one of dignity and usefulness. The man who fills it has in Scripture different titles expressive of his various duties. As he has the oversight of the flock of Christ, he is termed bishop or pastor. As it is his duty to be spiritually fruitful, dignified, and prudent, an example to the flock, and to govern well in the house and Kingdom of Christ, he is termed presbyter or elder. As he expounds the Word, and by sound doctrine both exhorts and convinces the gainsayer, he is termed teacher. These titles do not indicate different grades of office, but all describe one and the same office."},"source":{"name":"PCA Constitution Reader","revision":"edce8a8dcd9ced63bb585bf922e6a97319ef62e1","edition":"Current Reader text","files":{"bco.js":"c88e552545b73fd9690de620b237895b7ea52a94bed8e95690c116bf76be8ae5","wcf.js":"1ebf9e54223f7fe4e728a3e640c833a435af825d74b5ef3d4b04687685538a0d","wlc.js":"f6977e761ea4ccc93b07fcacfd0391890cb05b42